# Rianell architecture guard

## Dependency direction (hard rule)

- `packages/*` must **never** import from `apps/*`
- Apps import shared code only via `@rianell/*` package names or synced assets (tokens, i18n JSON)
- Scripts may import `@rianell/*` and `@rianell/build-tools`

```js
// ❌ WRONG — package importing an app
import { thing } from '../../apps/pwa-webapp/app.js';

// ✅ CORRECT — app importing a package
import { thing } from '@rianell/shared';
```

## Where new code lives

| Need | Location |
|------|----------|
| New deployable UI | `apps/<name>/` + workspace entry |
| Shared library | `packages/<name>/` with `@rianell/<name>` scope |
| Build / verify automation | `scripts/<concern>/` |
| User-facing docs | `wiki/` |
| Dev / security docs | `docs/` |

## Naming conventions

- Directories: **kebab-case**, no spaces (`artifacts/` not `App build/`)
- npm scope: always `@rianell/`
- Script categories: `scripts/<concern>/` (build, i18n, verify, ci, audit, wiki, models, dev)

## Workspace rules

- Python `server/` is **not** a JS workspace — do not add it to `workspaces` in root `package.json`
- `i18n-packs/` stays at repo root — do not move into `packages/`
- **No nested `package-lock.json`** under any workspace directory (CI guards this from Phase 13)
- Generated files (`app.*.min.js`, `asset-manifest.json`, `.server-dist/`) are never source of truth
